  "content": {
    "id": "p11-q10-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "A rope hangs from the top of a flag pole. The rope is 3 metres longer than the pole, and when it is pulled tight and held to the ground, the rope makes an angle of $50^\\circ$ to the horizontal. How tall is the flag pole? Give your answer to two decimal places.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p11-q10-short-result",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "9.82\\text{ m}",
                "display": false
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p11-q10-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "For pole height ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "h",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ", use ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\sin50^\\circ=\\frac{h}{h+3}",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ".",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let $h$ metres be the height of the pole. The rope is the hypotenuse and has length $(h+3)$ metres.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin50^\\circ&=\\frac{h}{h+3}\\\\(h+3)\\sin50^\\circ&=h\\\\h\\sin50^\\circ+3\\sin50^\\circ&=h\\\\h-h\\sin50^\\circ&=3\\sin50^\\circ\\\\h(1-\\sin50^\\circ)&=3\\sin50^\\circ\\\\h&=\\frac{3\\sin50^\\circ}{1-\\sin50^\\circ}\\\\h&\\approx9.82\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe flag pole is $9.82\\text{ m}$ tall.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 52
  },
